> **§4.1.1 Background Independence and the Modular Clock**
>
> A natural objection is that E_mod and σ₁(K_ξ) are defined using a modular generator and a clock gap that already carry units of energy and time, so the construction appears to smuggle in the time it claims to construct. We address this directly.
>
> *What is background-independent:* The modular generator K_ξ = −ln Δ_ρ is defined intrinsically from the local state ω and the algebra A(V) alone, with no reference to a background metric or external time. The dispersion σ₁(K_ξ) is a dimensionless Lorentz scalar (Theorem 4.1, Appendix D). The Fisher–Rao arc length ds_QFI is likewise computed purely from the state manifold.
>
> *What is background-dependent:* The calibration scale E_mod = max(ℏω₀, 2πk_B T_U) introduces a physical energy scale. At a = 0, E_mod = ℏω₀ is set by the atomic transition frequency, which is an *input* of the clock (not of the theory). At horizons, E_mod = 2πk_B T_U is set by the Unruh temperature, which is itself derived from the local acceleration via the Bisognano–Wichmann theorem.
